# DS3004: a glob that matches nothing. The note explains `*` and `**`.
mode: check
---- query
from '../../data/logs/*.csv' | take 1;
from '../../data/*.ndjson' | take 1;
from '../../data/**/*.tsv' | take 1
---- expected
error[DS3004]: no files match `../../data/logs/*.csv`
  --> query:1:6
  |
1 | from '../../data/logs/*.csv' | take 1;
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this pattern matched nothing
  |
  = note: `*` and `?` match within one directory; to match files in subdirectories too, use `**`, such as `'logs/**/*.csv'`

error[DS3004]: no files match `../../data/*.ndjson`
  --> query:2:6
  |
2 | from '../../data/*.ndjson' | take 1;
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this pattern matched nothing
  |
  = note: `*` and `?` match within one directory; to match files in subdirectories too, use `**`, such as `'logs/**/*.csv'`

error[DS3004]: no files match `../../data/**/*.tsv`
  --> query:3:6
  |
3 | from '../../data/**/*.tsv' | take 1
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this pattern matched nothing
  |
  = note: `*` matches within one directory and `**` matches any number of directories
